course: dictionary
lesson: 623
title: One word, two meanings: Babel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Babel is a word with two lives. With a small b, babel is a noun meaning a confused noise of many voices talking at once. With a capital B, Babel is a name: the Tower of Babel, a story in the Bible.
explain: In the Tower of Babel story, people tried to build a tower up to heaven. God mixed up their language so they could not understand each other, and they spread over the earth. The story explains why people speak different languages.
explain: Use context to tell which meaning is meant. «The Babel story explains why people speak different languages.» Here Babel is the name of a story. If the sentence is about a classroom full of shouting, Babel means noise. Ask: is this sentence about a story, or about noise?
explain: Then swap in your meaning and check. «The classroom was a babel of voices» becomes «a confused noise of many voices», and it still makes sense. That tells you the small-b meaning is right.
fact: Babel with a small b (noun) means a confused noise of many voices talking at once.
fact: Babel with a capital B is the Tower of Babel, a story in Genesis in the Bible.
fact: In the story, God mixed up people's languages so they could not understand each other.
fact: «The Bible's story of the Tower of Babel was probably inspired by a real ziggurat in Babylon.» A ziggurat was a huge stepped tower in Babylon, and «probably» means the story may be based on it, but nobody is sure.
fact: Useful phrases: the Tower of Babel, a babel of voices, a babel of languages.
exercise: «The classroom was a babel of voices before the bell rang.» What does babel mean here? | A story about a king | *A confused noise of many voices talking at once | A quiet, empty room | A tall tower made of stone
exercise: In the Babel story, why did people stop understanding each other? | They ran out of food | *God mixed up their languages | They were too tired to talk | They all moved to a new country
exercise: In «The Babel story explains why people speak different languages», what kind of word is Babel? | *A proper noun, the name of a story | A noise | A verb meaning to speak | An adjective describing a language
test: «The Tower of Babel was probably inspired by a real ziggurat in Babylon.» What does probably tell you? | *The story may be based on a real tower, but it is not certain | The tower is certainly real and proven | The tower was built last year | The tower was a city in Spain
test: Which phrase describes a noisy market full of people talking at once? | a pair of gloves | *a babel of voices | a quiet library | a stone bridge
exam: «Christians see Pentecost, when Jesus' followers were understood in many languages, as the reversal of Babel.» What does reversal mean here? | A new language | *The opposite of what happened at Babel | A second copy of the Babel story | A loud noise
